1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,424
Narrator: Scenario 17. Infrastructure operations.

2
00:00:06,024 --> 00:00:16,872
B: Was the overnight reboot planned, or did the underlying host fail? I cannot find a maintenance notice, and the application team is asking for an explanation.

3
00:00:17,472 --> 00:00:27,360
A: It was not in our change calendar. The guest boot record shows a restart at 03:14 UTC, but we have not confirmed what triggered it.

4
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:35,592
B: Has the application recovered, or are we reporting only that the operating system and application process have started again?

5
00:00:36,192 --> 00:00:47,328
A: The process is running and health checks pass. We are still validating a complete business transaction and checking whether the interrupted background jobs resumed correctly.

6
00:00:47,928 --> 00:00:59,304
B: Please prioritize that validation. For the reboot investigation, can we distinguish an operating system shutdown from a hypervisor reset or host-level event?

7
00:00:59,904 --> 00:01:09,696
A: The guest logs end abruptly without a normal shutdown entry. That supports looking outside the guest, but it does not prove the host failed.

8
00:01:10,296 --> 00:01:20,160
B: Have you checked platform automation and administrator actions as well? A restart request could come from a policy or a manual operation.

9
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:31,248
A: I requested the hypervisor event history and audit records from the platform owner. I will compare them with the guest timestamp and note any clock difference.

10
00:01:31,848 --> 00:01:42,456
B: Good. Are other virtual machines on the same host affected? That may help define the scope without assuming they experienced the same failure.

11
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:53,568
A: The platform team is checking that. So far, monitoring shows no confirmed restart on the two neighboring guests, but we need the host events to verify.

12
00:01:54,168 --> 00:02:04,992
B: Please give us a business recovery update by 04:00 UTC and a separate investigation update by 06:00 UTC, even if the trigger is still unknown.

13
00:02:05,592 --> 00:02:16,584
A: I own both updates and will involve the application owner for transaction checks. We will preserve the logs and keep the cause unconfirmed until evidence supports it.
